00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.420
As well as creating Word documents from
scratch, there may be occasions where

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.430
you wish to use a preformatted template.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.740
This could be for a CV, poster, flyer,
newsletter, or even a letter template.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.020
To access the templates, you would simply
need to go to the File menu, click on

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.120
File and then select New from Template.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.840
Once you've clicked on that, it
will open up the template box.

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:25.424
This will allow you to select
from a wide range of templates.

00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:28.935
And as you can see a blank document
is still a template because it

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:33.254
has preformatting applied such
as the font, the font size, the

00:00:33.254 --> 00:00:35.114
borders, margins, et cetera.

00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:39.375
Other templates available, as you
can see are notes, there's calendar

00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:44.635
templates, there's cover letters, there
are CVs, there's journals, newsletters,

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:46.575
brochures and leaflet templates.

00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:50.365
So once you've selected the
template that you wish to use, you

00:00:50.365 --> 00:00:52.230
would simply double click on that.

00:00:52.589 --> 00:00:54.870
And then that will open up in Word.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:00.470
And once the document is open in
Word, you would then be able to add

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:04.010
your title and then change the text.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.110
As you can see, the text
is already in there.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.190
So it just allows you to go in,
click on each section and then you

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.720
could change the text within there.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.130
The thing to remember with templates is
it will automatically apply the formatting

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.050
in that section that is already on there.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.270
So in this section, the title.

00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:25.274
The title is Times New Roman, 39
so whatever you type in there.

00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:29.475
It will automatically apply the
Times New Roman new room, 39 and

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:33.164
other various formatting options
will automatically be applied.

00:01:33.315 --> 00:01:36.324
So that's always something to
remember that if you want to use

00:01:36.324 --> 00:01:40.934
a template, it can be difficult to
make changes to the template if it

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.524
isn't suitable for your purpose.

